Q: Build an object from an existing one using lombok A: <p>Use MapStruct and create a mapper:</p>
<pre><code>@Mapper
public interface BandMapper {

    Band bandCopy(Band band);
}
</code></pre>
<p>and you can, for example, add a <code>@Setter</code> on your field <code>name</code> and then use</p>
<pre><code>final BandMapper bandMapper = Mappers.getMapper(BandMapper.class); // or use dependency injection
final Band nirvana = bandMapper.bandCopy(rollingStones);
nirvana.setName(&quot;nirvana&quot;);
</code></pre>
<p>Simple and elegant. It will work independently of whether you use <code>@Builder</code> or not.</p>

Q: Is it possible have Jackson&#39;s ObjectMapper honor the configured serialization features when serializing a JsonNode? A: <h1>Solution</h1>
<p>Enable the <code>JsonNodeFeature.WRITE_PROPERTIES_SORTED</code> feature that was introduced since Jackson 2.16.0.</p>
<h2>References</h2>
<h3>GitHub issue</h3>
<p><a href="https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/issues/3965" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Add `JsonNodeFeature.WRITE_PROPERTIES_SORTED` for sorting `ObjectNode` properties on serialization · Issue #3965 · FasterXML/jackson-databind</a>.</p>
<h3>Source code: <code>JsonNodeFeature</code> enum</h3>
<p><a href="https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/blob/jackson-databind-2.16.0/src/main/java/com/fasterxml/jackson/databind/cfg/JsonNodeFeature.java" rel="nofollow noreferrer">jackson-databind/src/main/java/com/fasterxml/jackson/databind/cfg/JsonNodeFeature.java at jackson-databind-2.16.0 · FasterXML/jackson-databind · GitHub</a>: an excerpt (slightly modified: added <code>// &lt;…&gt;</code>):</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>// &lt;…&gt;
public enum JsonNodeFeature implements DatatypeFeature
{
// &lt;…&gt;
    /**
     * When writing {@code com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.JsonNode}s are Object properties
     * (for {@code ObjectNode}s) sorted alphabetically (using natural order of
     * {@link java.lang.String}) or not?
     * If not sorted, order is the insertion order; when reading this also means retaining
     * order from the input document.
     *&lt;p&gt;
     * Default value: {@code false}
     *
     * @since 2.16
     */
    WRITE_PROPERTIES_SORTED(false),
// &lt;…&gt;
}
</code></pre>
<h2>Draft examples</h2>
<h3>Common</h3>
<h4><code>pom.xml</code> file (partial excerpt)</h4>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;UTF-8&quot;?&gt;
&lt;project&gt;
    &lt;modelVersion&gt;4.0.0&lt;/modelVersion&gt;
    &lt;properties&gt;
        &lt;encoding&gt;UTF-8&lt;/encoding&gt;
        &lt;java.version&gt;25&lt;/java.version&gt;
        &lt;maven.version&gt;3.9.12&lt;/maven.version&gt;
        &lt;project.build.sourceEncoding&gt;${encoding}&lt;/project.build.sourceEncoding&gt;
        &lt;project.reporting.outputEncoding&gt;${encoding}&lt;/project.reporting.outputEncoding&gt;
        &lt;maven.compiler.release&gt;${java.version}&lt;/maven.compiler.release&gt;
        &lt;jackson.version&gt;2.16.0&lt;/jackson.version&gt;
    &lt;/properties&gt;
    &lt;dependencies&gt;
        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;com.fasterxml.jackson.core&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;jackson-databind&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;version&gt;${jackson.version}&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;
        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;com.fasterxml.jackson.core&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;jackson-core&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;version&gt;${jackson.version}&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;
    &lt;/dependencies&gt;
&lt;/project&gt;
</code></pre>
<h4>Program output</h4>
<p>The programs (the draft examples) produce the same output.<br />
The output:</p>
<pre><code>{&quot;a&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;b&quot;:&quot;2&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:&quot;3&quot;}
</code></pre>
<h3>Draft example #1: Using <code>ObjectMapper</code> class</h3>
<h4><code>Program</code> class</h4>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>// TODO: package &lt;…&gt;;

import com.fasterxml.jackson.core.JsonProcessingException;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.JsonNode;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.cfg.JsonNodeFeature;

public final class Program {
    public static void main() throws JsonProcessingException {
        final ObjectMapper objectMapper = new ObjectMapper();
        objectMapper.configure(JsonNodeFeature.WRITE_PROPERTIES_SORTED, true);

        final JsonNode jsonNode = objectMapper.createObjectNode()
            .put(&quot;c&quot;, &quot;3&quot;)
            .put(&quot;b&quot;, &quot;2&quot;)
            .put(&quot;a&quot;, &quot;1&quot;);
        System.out.println(objectMapper.writeValueAsString(jsonNode));
    }
}
</code></pre>
<h3>Draft example #2: Using <code>JsonMapper</code> class</h3>
<h4><code>Program</code> class</h4>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>// TODO: package &lt;…&gt;;

import com.fasterxml.jackson.core.JsonProcessingException;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.JsonNode;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.cfg.JsonNodeFeature;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.json.JsonMapper;

public final class Program {
    public static void main() throws JsonProcessingException {
        final JsonMapper jsonMapper = JsonMapper.builder()
            .enable(JsonNodeFeature.WRITE_PROPERTIES_SORTED)
            .build();

        final JsonNode jsonNode = jsonMapper.createObjectNode()
            .put(&quot;c&quot;, &quot;3&quot;)
            .put(&quot;b&quot;, &quot;2&quot;)
            .put(&quot;a&quot;, &quot;1&quot;);
        System.out.println(jsonMapper.writeValueAsString(jsonNode));
    }
}
</code></pre>
